The following are IPW programs that have been modified:

ipwmake
-------

Changed ipwmake so that if the Makedefs file doesn't exist but a SCCS 
directory does, it will try getting the Makedefs file out of sccs.


ipwman
------
Made following change so that ipwman works for local code:

# following line modified by K. Longley 7/9/90
#pdirs='bin etc lib'
pdirs='bin etc lib exp/kelly exp/danny'


lincom
------
BUG FIX: changed routine headers.c to write only one band of header to the
output image file in call to gethdrs().


mkbih
-----
In this copy of mkbih a different annotation string can be specified for each
band.  This fixes the bug in the original mkbih where the annotation for band 0
was repeated for each band.


shade
-----

Changed line in shadetbl.c:

 /* Following line changed 8/28/90 by K. Longley USEPA ERL-C:
  *
  *			shade[s][a] = mu * maxval + 0.5;
  *
  *		Removed addition of 0.5 to prevent rounding
  *		fpio library would not round if we were using fpvwrite instead
  *		of doing the mapping ourselves.
  */
			shade[s][a] = mu * maxval;

xim
---

Change to original IPW source:

Added -I$(OPENWINHOME)/share/include to C_SPECIAL in Makedefs to compile for
SUN Openwindows.


libipw
------

Changed IPW fpio routines:

fpclose.c:

/* Following line changed to prevent infinite loop by K.Longley 9/21/90:
 *	for (band = 0; band < p->nbands; band) {
 */
	for (band = 0; band < p->nbands; band++) {

fpvwrite.c:

	/* Changed 4/26/91 by K. Longley - recompute coefficient in	*/
	/* double precision to reduce error in pixel computation	*/
	/*		k1 = p->lininv[band][1];		 	*/
	/*		if (nbands == 1) {				*/
	/*			do {					*/
	/*				*pixp++ = (*bufp++ - k0) * k1;	*/
	/*			} while (--npixels > 0);		*/
	/*		}						*/
	/*		else {						*/
	/*			do {					*/
	/*				*pixp = (*bufp - k0) * k1;	*/
	/*				bufp += nbands;			*/
	/*				pixp += nbands;			*/
	/*			} while (--npixels > 0);		*/
	/*		}						*/
	/* Above code lines replaced by the following:			*/
	/*		double k2;					*/

			k2 = (p->maplen[band]-1) /
				(p->fmax[band] - p->fmin[band]);

			if (nbands == 1) {
				do {
					*pixp++ = (*bufp++ - k0) * k2;
				} while (--npixels > 0);
			}
			else {
				do {
					*pixp = (*bufp - k0) * k2;

					bufp += nbands;
					pixp += nbands;
				} while (--npixels > 0);
			}
		}
	/* end replacement */



Changed IPW geoh routine:

geohwrite.c:

	Changed all ftoa calls to dtoa - needed more digits when
writing out bline, bsamp, dline, dsamp.
